.TH PURR-TRAY 1 "August 2026" "purr 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
purr-tray \- System Tray Indicator & Background Update Monitor for Purr
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B purr-tray
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBpurr-tray\fR is a native Qt6/KDE StatusNotifierItem system tray indicator daemon for \fBpurr\fR (Project Tuki). It monitors pending updates across official Arch Linux repositories (\fBcheckupdates\fR / \fBpacman\fR), the Arch User Repository (\fByay -Qua\fR), and Flatpaks (\fBflatpak remote-ls --updates\fR), as well as unreferenced/EOL Flatpak runtimes (\fBflatpak uninstall --unused\fR).
.PP
The indicator displays dynamic, color-coded urgency halos:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGreen / Clean\fR: System is fully up to date.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBlue / Info\fR: Minor updates available (\(le 5 packages).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAmber / Medium\fR: Moderate update backlog (> 5 packages).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRed / Urgent\fR: Critical system components pending (e.g. \fIlinux\fR, \fIsystemd\fR, \fImesa\fR, \fInvidia\fR, \fIglibc\fR, \fIplasma-desktop\fR) or large backlog (> 20 packages).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOrange / Warning\fR: Unreferenced or EOL Flatpak runtimes detected.
.PP
It features an instant IPC trigger mechanism: when an upgrade or package installation occurs via the \fBpurr\fR CLI, the tray indicator immediately refreshes without waiting for the recurring timer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " \fIMINUTES\fR"
Sets the background update check interval in minutes (default: 60).
.TP
.BR \-\-initial\-delay " \fISECONDS\fR"
Sets the delay before the initial check after login in seconds (default: 15, allowing network stacks and VPNs to initialize).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Shows the help message and exits.
.SH CONTEXT MENU ACTIONS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUniversal System Upgrade (purr up)\fR: Opens terminal and runs full upgrade with auto-conflict resolution.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPrune Unsupported / EOL Flatpak Runtimes\fR: Automatically uninstalls obsolete SDKs and runtimes.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCheck Frequency...\fR: Interactive dialog to select check frequency (15m, 30m, 60m, 120m, 240m, 360m).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCheck Now\fR: Force an immediate background update scan.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCompanion Launchers\fR: Quick links to Bauh, Pamac Software Center, and Discover.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/purr/config.json
Stores user preferences for interval and initial delay.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/purr/refresh_trigger
Watched by QFileSystemWatcher to trigger debounced instant update re-checks.
